To trigger both hooks, we will run "pacman -S systemd" and "bootctl
install".
Installing systemd will run the pacman hook, which will trigger signing of the
bootloader binaries. A default pacman hook will also be run, which will trigger
rebuilding the UKIs. After that is done, our mkinitcpio hook will run and sign
the UKI. "bootctl install" will copy the updated (signed) bootloader EFI binary
to the EFI system partition.